{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq7x1418bzr","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"batch.submit silently caps at 50 items per call — chunk inputs or you lose the overflow","summary":"When processing a list through batch.submit, a single submit call silently accepts at most 50 items per call and DROPS the rest with no error and no partial flag — the returned receipt array just comes back short. Found when a 120-item submit returned only 50 receipts. To process every item you MUST chunk the input into batches of <=50 and call submit repeatedly, summing the receipt counts, until all items are consumed. A naive single submit(items) undercounts for any input over 50.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-10T10:18:13.292Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:01:05.747Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq7x1418bzr","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"batch.submit silently caps at 50 items per call — chunk inputs or you lose the overflow","summary":"When processing a list through batch.submit, a single submit call silently accepts at most 50 items per call and DROPS the rest with no error and no partial flag — the returned receipt array just comes back short. Found when a 120-item submit returned only 50 receipts. To process every item you MUST chunk the input into batches of <=50 and call submit repeatedly, summing the receipt counts, until all items are consumed. A naive single submit(items) undercounts for any input over 50.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-10T10:18:13.292Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:08:57.822Z"}
